WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.710
In 24 hours I built

2
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:06.810
an artificial intelligence agent.

3
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.250
The first Philips AI Hackathon LATAM:

4
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:11.710
91 teams from all of Latin America.

5
00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.150
My team won.

6
00:00:13.338 --> 00:00:16.048
Six months earlier,
I had joined as an intern.

7
00:00:16.088 --> 00:00:17.698
I'm Martín Bundy.

8
00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.588
I study Industrial Engineering

9
00:00:23.628 --> 00:00:24.748
and artificial intelligence.

10
00:00:24.788 --> 00:00:27.688
And I use AI to solve real problems.

11
00:00:27.988 --> 00:00:30.928
I'm from Panama.
Since I was a kid, when I got stuck,

12
00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.668
I found my own way forward.

13
00:00:33.138 --> 00:00:36.338
Today I do the same
with processes, data and agents.

14
00:00:36.988 --> 00:00:39.288
At Philips I work in
operational procurement,

15
00:00:39.938 --> 00:00:43.438
the team that moves every purchase
from end to end.

16
00:00:43.588 --> 00:00:44.988
That is where something clicked.

17
00:00:45.188 --> 00:00:48.428
Industrial Engineering taught me to work
with very different processes

18
00:00:48.468 --> 00:00:50.528
and to understand
everything that can happen

19
00:00:50.568 --> 00:00:52.268
in a large operation.

20
00:00:52.548 --> 00:00:57.338
My question is always how to optimize it:
cut lead times, improve KPIs.

21
00:00:57.388 --> 00:01:00.048
At Philips I tracked every
purchase with 4 KPIs

22
00:01:00.088 --> 00:01:03.748
and built a no-code dashboard.
No more manual reports.

23
00:01:03.788 --> 00:01:07.298
With AI I look to automate:
agents and custom-built software.

24
00:01:07.338 --> 00:01:08.718
AI helps me with everything:

25
00:01:08.758 --> 00:01:11.808
from my daily life to the
processes at Philips.

26
00:01:11.848 --> 00:01:14.948
In 2025 I led the AI integration

27
00:01:14.988 --> 00:01:18.664
of Conecta Panamá:
a citizen super app, in two weeks.

28
00:01:18.704 --> 00:01:22.804
I built the AI, the design, the interface,
the backend and the debugging.

29
00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:24.615
First place.

30
00:01:24.905 --> 00:01:26.025
The digital innovation team

31
00:01:26.065 --> 00:01:28.385
of the Municipality of
Panama wanted to apply it,

32
00:01:28.425 --> 00:01:31.625
and we sat down to plan
how to take it nationwide.

33
00:01:31.871 --> 00:01:34.171
I trained a university
assistant with BERT:

34
00:01:34.711 --> 00:01:37.161
it answers the questions that
used to arrive by email.

35
00:01:37.201 --> 00:01:39.701
I presented a logistics copilot live

36
00:01:39.741 --> 00:01:40.561
at Expo Logística,

37
00:01:40.601 --> 00:01:43.711
in front of transport,
cargo and 3PL companies.

38
00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:46.583
At Philips I built an agent
that answers in seconds

39
00:01:46.623 --> 00:01:48.633
and cites the exact source.

40
00:01:50.103 --> 00:01:54.653
Last year only Panama competed.
This year, all of Latin America.

41
00:01:54.693 --> 00:01:59.553
I led the team and built all of the AI
for PO Guru in 24 hours.

42
00:01:59.593 --> 00:02:02.573
4 minutes of pitch.
First place in Panama,

43
00:02:02.613 --> 00:02:04.333
out of about 30 teams.

44
00:02:04.373 --> 00:02:07.013
In the final, against
the best in the region,

45
00:02:07.053 --> 00:02:08.153
first place.

46
00:02:08.404 --> 00:02:10.404
I learned to work under pressure.

47
00:02:10.604 --> 00:02:15.334
I like to understand what people need,
connect the pieces, test and improve.

48
00:02:18.254 --> 00:02:19.534
What I learn, I teach:

49
00:02:19.574 --> 00:02:22.864
on tincho.ia I explain AI
and agents from scratch.

50
00:02:23.104 --> 00:02:26.904
My CV is a website I
designed and built with AI.

51
00:02:27.804 --> 00:02:30.704
And I directed this film with agents too.

52
00:02:35.204 --> 00:02:37.764
To me, AI is already the present.

53
00:02:37.804 --> 00:02:39.804
Everything is changing very fast,

54
00:02:40.804 --> 00:02:44.004
and learning to build
with agents is a wave.

55
00:02:45.054 --> 00:02:47.654
You either ride it, or
you get left behind.

56
00:02:54.054 --> 00:02:57.794
I like to dream big.
I don't box myself into one thing.

57
00:02:57.834 --> 00:03:00.134
I'm always open to new challenges.

58
00:03:02.054 --> 00:03:03.454
What's next...

59
00:03:04.854 --> 00:03:06.854
...I'll tell you in person.
